WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.027 --> 00:00:02.360
- [Zac] "Halloween III" is
known as the black sheep,

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.440
the "Tokyo Drift", the "Zelda II"

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.940
of the Halloween franchise.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.610
For that reason, the series connections,

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.410
we've now come to expect are more tenuous,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.940
but if we inspect the movie closely,

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.620
some of its hidden secrets
start to come into view.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.740
The story follows Dr. Daniel Challis,

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.950
who was called into the hospital

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.370
to take care of an injured patient

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.832
and prescribes a medication
called Thorazine.

00:00:21.832 --> 00:00:23.580
- 100 milligrams, Thorazine.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.200
- [Zac] This calls back
to the first "Halloween"

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.300
where Dr. Loomis plans
to use the same drug

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.170
to sedate Michael Myers.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.535
- What do I give him when we
take him in front of the judge?

00:00:31.535 --> 00:00:32.990
- Thorazine.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.541
- Barely be able to sit up.

00:00:34.541 --> 00:00:35.960
- That's the idea.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.240
- [Zac] After realizing the
suspicious circumstances

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.710
of the patient's death, Challis
decides to go investigate

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.530
with the man's daughter, Ellie Grimbridge.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:45.170
Before leaving town, he rings
his ex-wife at a payphone.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.360
This is the same location
featured in "Halloween II",

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.040
where the nurse, Karen, announces

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.279
that she never wants to go
to another Halloween party.

00:00:51.279 --> 00:00:53.600
- Especially not at Stevie Mathis's house.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.670
- [Zac] The biggest connection

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.420
to the original two
Halloween movies, though,

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.070
which many viewers are not aware of,

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:00.760
has to do with the reason that
the villain, Conal Cochran,

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.830
has put this elaborate plan into motion.

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.230
To learn the little known-connection

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.260
between him and Michael Myers,

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.643
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:08.643 --> 00:01:12.226
(heavy metal music begins)

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:16.479
- [TV commercial] Three
more weeks till Halloween,

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:18.570
Halloween, Halloween.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.280
Three more weeks till
Halloween, Silver Shamrock.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.010
- Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:26.670
Just one year after killing
off the popular slasher,

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.990
Michael Myers, series
producers John Carpenter

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:30.990
and Debra Hill were
interested in continuing

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.510
with their original idea
of an anthology series.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.490
Where each movie would
tell an unrelated story

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.976
taking place on Halloween night.

00:01:36.976 --> 00:01:39.080
As always I'll be joined in this video

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.320
by the literal prime
minister of Haddonfield,

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.890
Jimmy Champane.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:43.787
- It's commonly thought that

00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:45.400
"Halloween III: Season of the Witch"

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.510
is the only movie in
the Halloween franchise

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.080
that doesn't feature Michael Myers

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.860
But that's not exactly true.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.200
We see Michael in a commercial
for a television airing

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.980
of the original
"Halloween", which tells us

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.900
that "Halloween" is only
a movie in this universe.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.510
- [Zac] Tommy Lee Wallace was excited by

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.440
the prospect of getting
to tell a new story.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.570
So after declining to
take over "Halloween II"

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.990
he signed down as the director
of the third installment.

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:07.270
That's actually his voice in the

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.722
Silver Shamrock commercials.

00:02:08.722 --> 00:02:09.850
- [TV announcer] All you lucky kids

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.012
with Silver Shamrock masks

00:02:11.012 --> 00:02:15.540
gather around your TV set,
put on your masks and watch.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.140
- I learned this while trying to determine

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.170
if this was the same
voice as Dr. Dementia,

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.060
the horror movie marathon
host in the first two films.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.377
- [TV Host] Lock your
doors, bolt your windows

00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:28.470
and turn off the lights.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.420
- They're similar, but
I never did find out

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.480
if Dr. Dementia was voiced by Tommy.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.960
- I mean, I haven't heard otherwise.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.097
So let's just go with it.

00:02:35.097 --> 00:02:37.100
- [Zac] "Halloween III" is a weird movie,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.100
but the same oddities
that turned off critics

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.350
and fans in the early eighties

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.970
are part of what makes it a
cult classic decades later.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.120
With that all being said,

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.161
let's get into the things you missed.

00:02:46.161 --> 00:02:47.268
(knives sharpening)

00:02:47.268 --> 00:02:51.194
(dramatic music beginning)

00:02:51.194 --> 00:02:53.100
- [Zac] The opening credits are displayed

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.080
over a series of lines, appearing close up

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.200
on a TV screen.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.760
We don't know it yet,
but what we're seeing

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.810
is a very zoomed in version of the video

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.490
that triggers the brainwash sequence.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.910
I love how right from the first shot,

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.300
you already know this
movie is going to be funny

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.940
and just the way that this
guy runs makes me laugh.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.010
An hour later, he arrives at a gas station

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.110
where we see the news report

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.130
about the missing Stonehenge monument.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:13.510
- [TV announcer] It
weighs more than five tons

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:16.170
making its disappearance a mystery indeed.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.990
- I'm not exactly sure why Cochran felt

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.360
like he needed to steal
the entire giant stone,

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.610
because he only ended up
using like a small chunk

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.420
of that monument to enact his plan.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.010
Wouldn't it be smarter just
to take the chunk you need

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.920
instead of removing an
entire ancient monument?

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.380
I get that we find out that all you need

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.610
is an extremely small
speck to do major damage

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:35.110
and that's what ends up in every single

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.260
Silver Shamrock mask.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.530
But still the amount
they're using in these masks

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.470
is absolutely tiny compared
to that massive monument,

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.490
which everyone realized was stolen.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.050
- [Zac] So the Stonehenge news
report sets up the big reveal

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.190
about what the company's
true intentions are.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:50.937
But the next program after
this is also significant.

00:03:50.937 --> 00:03:52.720
- [Radio announcer] When we
come back Trina will be here

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.110
to tell you what you
can do about junk mail.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:55.960
Stay with us.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.330
- [Zac] Junk mail is a form
of overbearing advertising,

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.490
which ties into the main
message of this movie.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.875
The entire crux of Cochran's
plan relies on children

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.940
to be brainwashed by the Silver Shamrock

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:06.460
commercials that dominate the airwaves

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:07.950
in the days leading up to Halloween.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.310
Michael Myers may not show up

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.840
to chase any teenagers this time,

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.880
but Daniel Challis is constantly chased

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.600
by this catchy yet annoying
Silver Shamrock jingle.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.040
Almost every location
in the movie has screens

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.580
or radios manipulating
children to buy their masks

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.910
and wear them on the big
Halloween night giveaway.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.770
There are so many screens,
I started to wonder

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.480
if I wasn't at Universal Studios.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.600
That's a stupid joke.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.660
- We are totally joking.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.930
Universal please let us come
to Halloween Horror Nights

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:31.763
this year.

00:04:31.763 --> 00:04:33.440
- [Zac] Just as the first
Halloween makes a comment

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.637
about the sexual revolution
still ongoing from the 1960's,

00:04:36.637 --> 00:04:38.400
"Season of the Witch" taps into concerns

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.290
of the effects of television on children.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.040
A discussion that was
still picking up steam

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.710
from the late 1970s.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.180
Even though television is
no longer a relevant medium

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.000
for young people, the themes
of this movie remain pertinent.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.560
It was not that long ago that YouTube

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.680
implemented strict rules regarding content

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.800
made for children to make sure
that they aren't subjected

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:55.980
to targeted advertising.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.280
And also a bunch of other lame
restrictions for some reason.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.700
Let's just say it was the only
time, ever, where operating

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.070
a horror themed channel actually paid off.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.270
- Yo Zac, let's make a
Cocomelon horror movie.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.280
- Yeah, I'm sure that
won't get us struck down

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.515
off YouTube immediately.

00:05:08.515 --> 00:05:09.720
(dramatic musical note plays)

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.580
We see the effects of over advertising

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.680
towards kids on Challis's own offspring.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.520
They each get Silver Shamrock masks

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.028
and huddle around the TV
when the commercial comes on.

00:05:18.028 --> 00:05:22.111
(Silver Shamrock Jingle playing)

00:05:25.994 --> 00:05:27.240
- [TV Announcer] Yes, kids you too,

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:29.640
can own one of the big Halloween three.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.750
That's right, three horrific
masks to choose from.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:35.200
- The masks are marketed
as the big Halloween three.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.730
Yes, let's go ahead and get our jokes in

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.870
about the title of the
movie being in the movie.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.470
And there are many threes or triples

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.050
in this movie and I'm not sure how many

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:43.010
of them are intentional.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.380
So I'm just going to show
them and let you decide.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:47.760
Also of note, the deadly
Silver Shamrock program

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.120
at the end is airing on
three different channels.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.620
There are, perhaps, other
number games at play here.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.280
Mr. Grimbridge's room at
the hospital is room 13.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:57.150
If you've seen my final destination videos

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.270
you know all about how
that's the unlucky number,

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:01.810
but, in this case, it's
also the reverse of 31.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:04.180
As in October 31, Halloween night.

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.640
There are also a lot of
instances of the number six.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.520
The motel room that
Challis and Ellie stay in

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.510
is room six, the town's curfew
goes into effect at 6:00 PM,

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:14.330
and the activation code for
the commercial is 6, 6, 6.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.400
The number of the devil.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.740
It's not just the numbers that
we should be paying attention

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:18.573
to though.

00:06:18.573 --> 00:06:21.080
There are also several names
that have a deeper meaning

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.606
than what meets the eye.

00:06:22.606 --> 00:06:27.606
- (scary, intense music begins)

00:06:27.755 --> 00:06:31.520
- (creepy music begins)

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.210
- [Zac] When chalice gets to the hospital,

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:35.770
his new patient is Harry
Grimbridge, a shop owner

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.130
who apparently discovered
the Silver Shamrock secret

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.120
and was hunted down by
the androids who worked

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.090
for Mr. Cochran.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.010
The assassin promptly leaves the hospital

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:45.876
and gets into his Plymouth
Fury and self-destructs.

00:06:45.876 --> 00:06:47.453
(car exploding)

00:06:47.453 --> 00:06:49.730
(car exploding)

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.510
- Seeing as John Carpenter
produced this movie

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.710
and was absolutely
instrumental in getting it made

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.210
this might've been yet another hint

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.350
as to what one of his
future projects would be.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.617
That's because his adaptation
of the Stephen King novel,

00:06:59.617 --> 00:07:01.480
"Christine", would come
out a few years later.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.320
For those of you who don't
know what that's about,

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:06.190
it's about a kid who buys
a cursed 1958 Plymouth,

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.430
and then ends up destroying
it because it has a mind

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:10.150
of its own and starts killing people.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.580
Now the car in "Halloween
III", isn't an exact match,

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.070
but it's the same make and model

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:16.240
so I feel like it's worth
bringing up nonetheless.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.840
Before you light us up
down in the comments,

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.190
I know that John Carpenter
has said multiple times

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.290
over the years, that this
is his least favorite movie

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.220
that he's ever made.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.110
But I've also seen
recently that he started

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.080
to come around on it.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.690
So yeah, I absolutely love it.

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:28.980
And I watch it all the time.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.800
I'm glad he's starting in like it too.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.190
- Is there also a second
Stephen King connection

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:34.401
in "Season of the witch"?

00:07:34.401 --> 00:07:36.980
Probably not, but I'm going
to mention it anyways.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.520
Inside Mr. Grimbridge's store

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.580
there are these Jack in
the Box clowns in a box

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.880
that says boats.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.250
Director Tommy Lee Wallace
would go on to direct

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:47.187
a production where a creepy
clown steals a young boys boat.

00:07:47.187 --> 00:07:49.010
"It" would not come out
for another eight years,

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:49.843
however.

00:07:49.843 --> 00:07:50.840
So I'm just going to chalk this one up

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:52.470
to just being a fun coincidence.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.610
Perhaps a more intentional
detail can be seen

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.410
when Ellie is brought in to ID her father

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:57.280
after his death.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.740
The county Sheriff's name
badge reads Dunsmuir.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.150
Dunsmuir is a small town
in northern California,

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:04.720
much like Santa Mira, where
the movie takes place.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.340
I wouldn't be surprised if Dunsmuir

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.490
was one of the inspirations
for this location

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.240
though it seems a little bit less creepy

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.610
than it's film counterpart.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:13.680
Santa Mira is named after a fictional town

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.730
from an earlier Sci-Fi
horror movie and novel

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.560
called "Invasion of the Body Snatchers."

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.870
This was the start of a trend.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.560
A lot of other properties would borrow

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.320
this fictional location for their setting,

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.090
including "AirWolf", "The Dark Tower",

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:26.060
and even the "Sharknado" franchise.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.600
Challis hangs out in a bar where
he is once again, bombarded

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.750
by the overplayed
Halloween mask commercial.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.300
He asks the bartender
to change the channel

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.230
and he puts on a football
game, which we can hear

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:36.720
in the background as Ellie
Grimbridge introduces herself.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.629
Listen to the names called
out by the announcer,

00:08:38.629 --> 00:08:41.240
- [TV announcer] ...Bernardi
finally brought him down,

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:44.000
not much time to do anything, but
coach Tommy Marshall has been...

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.960
- These are both
references to crew members

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:46.793
of the movie.

00:08:46.793 --> 00:08:48.270
Barry Bernardi was an associate producer

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:50.410
and Tommy Marshall was
best boy electrician.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.170
There are a few more crew
reference Easter eggs

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.210
that I spotted in the guest
book when Challis and Ellie

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:57.290
get to the hotel, including
costumer, Frances Vega Aubrey,

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:59.970
who signs as both Francis
Aubrey and Mr. F Vega

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:02.120
and property master James Rathbun.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.070
- [Jimmy] Last episode when
we covered "Halloween II",

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.100
I mentioned how Nancy
Loomis, also known as

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.120
Nancy Kyes or Keys, I'm not exactly

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.180
sure how to say it, appears in each movie

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.710
in the original Halloween trilogy.

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:12.920
This time she plays none other

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:15.190
than Dr. Dan Challis's ex-wife, Linda.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.830
I've seen this movie like 20 times,

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:18.690
and I never connected that Linda is played

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.120
by the same actress as Annie.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.030
Mainly, because she comes
off like such a huge *****.

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:25.070
Another actress who appears
in each of the first three

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:27.300
Halloween movies is Laurie Strode herself,

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.210
Jamie Lee Curtis.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.590
Because we of course, see her
during the television airing

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:32.044
of "Halloween" in this movie.

00:09:32.044 --> 00:09:33.893
(creepy music begins)

00:09:33.893 --> 00:09:35.540
(glass breaking)

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:37.820
- [Zac] I guess Dr. Challis is not a fan.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:40.393
The other Jamie Lee Curtis
cameo is a bit more covert.

00:09:40.393 --> 00:09:42.880
It is her voice that
announces the early curfew

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:43.713
in Santa Mira.

00:09:43.713 --> 00:09:44.566
(haunting music begins)

00:09:44.566 --> 00:09:47.655
- [public address announcer]
It's 6 o'clock. It's 6 o'clock.

00:09:47.655 --> 00:09:50.210
Curfew. Curfew.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.330
- There's one other
notable cameo appearance

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:53.890
and it comes from Dick Warlock.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:56.530
This is the guy who played
Michael Myers in "Halloween II".

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:58.230
So we see him unmasked for the first time

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.600
when he appears as one of
Conal Cochran's Androids.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.930
I know I don't normally
talk about actor cameos

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.560
and things you missed,
but it felt relevant

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.710
to bring up since this
is a spiritual successor

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.810
to the first two movies.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:09.740
It's kind of like how "Shock
Treatment" is a followup

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:10.700
to "Rocky Horror".

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.380
Similar crew, similar cast,

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.290
similar artwork, and feel, but totally

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:15.140
different story.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:17.120
On the drive to Santa
Mira, Challis and Ellie

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.320
read up on the town.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.160
- [Challis] Proud community,
predominantly Irish.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.300
- [Ellie] Irish Halloween masks?

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.350
- [Challis] In California, you never know.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.930
- Outside of the company
producing the mask

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.110
being called Silver Shamrock,

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:31.100
there are a lot of references
to Ireland and Irish culture.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.860
So let's just go over all of them

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.320
to make sure we've got our bases covered.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.360
Dr. Challis and that weirdo he meets

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.820
both appear to be alcoholics.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:39.450
Heavy drinking is a common trait

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.230
of the stereotypical Irishman.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:43.830
- Drinking and doctoring,
great combination.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.470
- Another thing Irish people are known for

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.160
can be seen in this clip.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.638
(car exploding)

00:10:48.638 --> 00:10:49.890
*laughter*

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.630
- [Zac] The bar he hangs
out at is decorated

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.650
with Irish murals.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.320
For example, this one on the back wall

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.770
is a depiction of Anne Bonny,

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.800
an Irish pirate from the 1700s.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.180
The other businesses in Santa Mira

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:00.820
are also themed to Irish culture.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.600
Rafferty is a classic Irish name.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.250
Dublin is the capital of Ireland.

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:06.290
The word shamrock is kind of overused.

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:08.730
In addition to the factory,
there's also a Shamrock Store

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.050
and a Shamrock Savings.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.730
Though personally, I would have
gone with Leprechaun Loans.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.950
They ended up staying at
the Rose of Shannon Motel.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:17.460
A reference to the town of
Shannon in Western Ireland.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.430
The booking office has
a huge map of Ireland

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:20.470
hanging on the wall.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:22.990
The Kupfer family arrives
at the motel in a big RV

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:23.970
covered in stickers.

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.530
It's hard to make them
out, but one of them

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.760
definitely has the
colors of the Irish flag.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:30.140
While touring the factory,
we learn that Silver Shamrock

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.740
used to be known for making toys,

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:33.220
like these windup machines.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:35.570
This one depicts a group of
musically inclined insects

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.580
called the Lovebug Band,
which is a reference

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:40.420
to an Irish pop band from the
eighties known as Luv Bug.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.830
The depiction of them as
insects may also be a connection

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.470
to the method by which the Halloween masks

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.310
kill the children.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:47.450
They're zapped by this laser
from the Stonehenge piece,

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.830
which causes their brains to
turn into a swarm of insects

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.320
that come pouring out of their heads.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.940
I don't care what you
think about this movie,

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.350
you gotta love that kill.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:55.720
- [Jimmy] It's a great practical gag

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.570
because you see it happen in real time,

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.940
but it's not actually that
hard to throw together.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.210
- Finally, there's the big
reveal about why Cochran

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:03.360
is targeting children.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.419
I'm going to turn on the subtitles and

00:12:05.419 --> 00:12:06.623
- Alright, roll it.

00:12:08.293 --> 00:12:11.746
- It was the start of the
year in our old Celtic lands

00:12:11.746 --> 00:12:16.746
and we'd be waiting in our
houses of wattles and clay.

00:12:17.034 --> 00:12:19.382
The barriers would be down, you see,

00:12:19.382 --> 00:12:21.613
between the real and the unreal,

00:12:22.854 --> 00:12:25.320
and the dead might be looking in

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:27.352
to sit by our fires of turf.

00:12:27.352 --> 00:12:31.200
(dramatic music rising)

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:32.080
Halloween...

00:12:34.836 --> 00:12:37.200
the festival of Samhain!

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.033
- Did you catch that?

00:12:38.033 --> 00:12:40.530
Although Cochran says it
differently than Dr. Sam Loomis

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.910
did in "Halloween II",
he tells us that children

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.080
are sacrificed during
the festival of Samhain.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.090
Remember how Michael
defaced the chalkboard

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:48.920
leading Loomis to believe that his crimes

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:49.930
were part of a tribute?

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:52.230
It turns out that Cochran's
plan to eviscerate the minds

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:53.440
of American trick-or-treaters

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.010
comes from a similar motivation.

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:56.590
Which makes this the only through line

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.710
between "Halloween II"
and "Halloween III".

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.970
- There is another hint
about the true purpose

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:03.830
of the Silver Shamrock masks
hidden in one small detail

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:05.018
at the motel.

00:13:05.018 --> 00:13:08.965
(intense scary music begins)

00:13:08.965 --> 00:13:12.132
(creepy music begins)

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.490
- No "Halloween III"
video would be complete

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:19.560
without making fun of
the mature relationship

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.760
between Dr. Challis and Ellie Grimbridge.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:23.780
I mean, her father just
died earlier that week

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:25.940
and she's already trying to
get it on with a mustached man,

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.660
literally more than twice her age.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.960
Seriously, you're going to
investigate your father's murder,

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:31.660
why did you even pack that outfit?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.070
It's so ridiculous.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.000
- [Jimmy] Playing an older guy
who gets with younger girls

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.540
is exactly what Tom Atkins was born to do.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.290
I mean, have you seen The Fog.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.840
- And I'm not even making this up,

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.180
but I was looking into this movie

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:43.870
and learned that the scenes in Santa Mira

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:46.770
were filmed at a place
called Loleta, California.

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:50.460
- I do love a good joke
and this is the best ever.

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.410
- Despite how unintentionally funny

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:53.740
this movie can be at times,

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:56.566
and believe me, it can
be unintentionally funny.

00:13:56.566 --> 00:14:01.566
(Silver Shamrock
commercial jingle playing)

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.560
- But despite all of that,
the way the mystery's set up

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.480
is actually really well done.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.180
Or at least kind of well done.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:12.130
There are a lot of details
that set up the fact

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.630
that the factory workers are robots,

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:16.120
like the explanation
of the hiring process.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.543
- He brought in every damn
one of them factory people

00:14:18.543 --> 00:14:20.470
from the outside.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:22.417
Think he'd hire me, a local boy?

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.100
No way, turned me down flat.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:26.830
- And the realization that the initial

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:29.860
assassin's autopsy only
contains machine parts.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.600
- We've been doing an
autopsy on part of the car.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.310
- It's still hilarious
when you first hear it.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.650
There's also a little foreshadowing

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.710
about the magic element of Cochran's plan.

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:40.280
At the motel a woman named
Marge Guttman can be seen

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.720
reading Carlos Castaneda's
"The Eagles Gift."

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:45.450
From what I understand
this book is about sorcery.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.420
Although the magic used to sacrifice

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:50.040
the mask wearing children is
referred to as witchcraft,

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.370
and although one of the
big Halloween three masks

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:55.540
is a witch, there isn't an
actual witch in the movie.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.160
I read somewhere that Tommy Lee Wallace

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.540
named it after the Donovan
song "Season of the Witch".

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.100
Great song, but it is
also not in the movie.

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:04.430
The finale shows us kids
going out to trick-or-treat

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:06.160
all over the country, which by the way,

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.700
includes some beautiful shots
of the Halloween sunset.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:10.700
Challis rescues what he thinks is Ellie,

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.850
but actually turns out to be robo Ellie.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:15.000
Not sure how or why Cochran had the time

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.070
to make a perfect replica
of her just to screw

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:19.810
with old Challis or why
the robo Ellie never tries

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:22.230
to stop him until after
he's destroyed the factory.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.010
But whatever, I'm into this.

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:26.310
(threatening music begins)

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:28.430
- [Jimmy] I got to say, I love
this movie's generous take

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:31.080
on how many cities actually
celebrate Halloween anymore.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:33.160
I mean, I've lived in L.A. five years

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.920
and I've never once had a kid come to

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:36.790
my door to trick-or-treat on Halloween.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.180
- Yeah, I was disappointed to
see the lack of decorations

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.860
on most houses when I moved out here.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:43.370
After fighting her off, he
inexplicably leaves the car

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:45.920
behind and goes to the gas
station where the movie started

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.510
to try to get the hypnotic
advert taken off the air.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.470
Who goes trick or
treating at a gas station?

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:52.960
Apparently these kids do,
and they gather around the TV

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:55.560
as Dr. Challis begs the
programmer to take the commercial

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:57.633
off of the three channels
that it's airing on.

00:15:57.633 --> 00:16:01.070
- Wait, you never went trick
or treating at a gas station?

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:03.830
- Do they get out gas or candy?

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:05.910
- I don't remember.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:07.630
- This brings us back to the main theme

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.520
that I discussed about "Halloween III".

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:12.530
The Silver Shamrock advert
is representative of every TV

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:15.040
commercial attempting to
corrupt and brainwash the youth

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:18.010
into becoming their ideal
consumer, regardless of any harm

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.750
that this might be
doing to them physically

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:21.030
or psychologically.

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:22.520
The bugs and snakes that pour out

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:24.320
of the young Kupfer boys head are symbolic

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:26.180
of what is going on inside
the heads of children

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:28.200
who were exposed to
overbearing advertising

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:29.210
from a young age.

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.590
The parents of these kids
do show some concern,

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.560
saying things like "don't sit too close"

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.420
or "turn down the volume", but ultimately

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:37.950
the kids are drawn to the
flashy colors and catchy tunes

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:38.940
of the broadcast.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:41.140
During the factory tour, we
learned that Silver Shamrock

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:43.640
used to be a toy manufacturer
and eventually switched

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.930
to hypnotic masks and television programs.

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:47.990
In the 1980's, when
this movie takes place,

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:50.250
television was reaching
the peak of its popularity

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.950
and Cochran was just
following what the kids

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:52.990
were paying attention to.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.350
TV shows were the new
toys and Silver Shamrock

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:58.040
is a stand in for any number
of malicious private companies

00:16:58.040 --> 00:16:59.610
ready to take advantage of that.

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:01.920
- Like most good movie
satire, "Halloween III"

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:03.030
was ahead of its time.

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:04.820
I think it's because it's
hard to notice that stuff

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.550
when it's still happening all around you,

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:08.740
but then when you revisit
a movie a few years later,

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:11.110
all of the satirical jokes
hit you right on the head.

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:12.587
It's kind of funny that 40 years later,

00:17:12.587 --> 00:17:15.120
"Stranger Things 3" covered
the exact same stuff

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:16.240
as Halloween 3.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.560
- Yes and I'll definitely have
to think about covering that

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:21.289
on my channel sometime soon as well.

00:17:21.289 --> 00:17:22.122
Hint.

00:17:22.122 --> 00:17:25.010
But if the years since 1978
have taught us anything,

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:27.200
it's that you can't kill Michael Myers.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:30.480
And even if you could, he
just won't stay dead for long.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.600
The Halloween anthology
concept was abandoned

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.450
after the poor reception
of "Halloween III",

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.970
and in 1988, the prolific
slasher would wake up

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.860
and set his sights on a new target.

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:41.030
Which means we've got more
things you missed to discuss

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:44.090
in "Halloween 4: The
Return of Michael Myers".

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:46.127
Meanwhile, there is a new Halloween movie,

00:17:46.127 --> 00:17:48.500
"Halloween Kills", just one week away.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.570
Jimmy has been covering
everything related to Kills

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:53.070
lately on his channel so head
over there and drop him a sub.

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:54.339
Otherwise he'll be forced to

00:17:54.339 --> 00:17:57.413
[TV Commercial] ♪ Subscribe to
Jimmy Champane! Mee Champane!

00:17:57.413 --> 00:18:02.050
Mee Champane! Subscribe to Jimmy
Champane, on his YouTube! ♪

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:03.790
- [Zac] And click that video on the left

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:05.930
and if you love Halloween,
make sure to subscribe

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:08.140
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:10.360
Ring the death bell for all notifications,

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.430
and I'll see you in the next one,

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:14.899
assuming we both survive.

00:18:14.899 --> 00:18:19.899
(slow creepy version of
Silver Shamrock jangle fading)

